\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid548598 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\kerning2\loch\af31506\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid548598\charrsid548598 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 I recently completed an end-to-end credit risk analytics project focused on a question every lender faces: which customers are likely to miss their next payment?
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
Using more than 30,000 credit card records from the UCI Machine Learning Repository, I developed a solution in Python covering the full workflow: automated data validation and quality reporting, a logistic regression model estimating each customer's proba
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
bility of default, Low / Medium / High risk segmentation with adjustable thresholds, per-customer explanations of the main risk drivers, batch scoring with Excel output, and an interactive dashboard designed for non-technical users.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Results on held-out data
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
The model achieved a ROC-AUC of 0.76. Its probabilities were well calibrated, with an average estimate of 22.3% against an actual default rate of 22.1%. The risk segments also held up in practice: customers classified as high risk, with an average estimat
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 e of 70%, defaulted at a rate of 68%.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Key observations
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Accuracy can be misleading on imbalanced data. The model reached 82% accuracy, but a baseline predicting no defaults scores 78%. Recall, precision and calibration give a more meaningful assessment.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
Threshold selection is a business decision. At a 50% cut-off, the model identifies about one third of future defaulters, with two thirds of its alerts being correct. A lower threshold captures more defaulters at the cost of more false alerts. The dashboar
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 d allows decision-makers to evaluate this trade-off directly.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Recent payment behaviour is the strongest predictor. Customers two or more months behind in the most recent month defaulted at a rate of 69%, compared with 17% for all others.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Explainability supports adoption. Each estimate is presented in plain terms, for example "about 66 out of 100 similar customers missed a payment," together with its main contributing factors.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
Responsible use requires care. The dataset contains demographic attributes such as gender, age and marital status. Any production lending application would require fairness testing and legal review before using such inputs.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Tools: Python, pandas, scikit-learn, Plotly, REST/JSON API, HTML/CSS/JavaScript,\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506  pytest (50 automated tests).
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 I would welcome perspectives from professionals in credit risk and analytics, particularly on approaches to threshold selection and model explainability in practice.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Data source: UCI Machine Learning Repository (Yeh & Lien, 2009).
