\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1640749\charrsid1640749 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 I recently completed an end-to-end credit risk analytics project focused on a question every lender faces: which customers are likely to miss their next payment?

\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
The analysis is based on more than 30,000 real credit card customers of a bank in Taiwan, covering April to September 2005 and published by the UCI Machine Learning Repository. For each customer, the data includes their credit limit, selected personal det
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 ails, six months of repayment status, bill amounts and payments, and whether they missed the following month's payment.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
Using this data, I developed a solution in Python covering the full workflow: automated data validation and quality reporting, with the original source files only ever read and never modified; a logistic regression model estimating each customer's probabi
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
lity of default; Low / Medium / High risk segmentation with adjustable thresholds; per-customer explanations of the main risk drivers; batch scoring with Excel output; and an interactive dashboard designed for non-technical users.
